{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Rethem</b> — By the way of the language it ought to be רתמי, and the meaning is 'bound,' and so it is the way of travelers to bind a rethem. Or the meaning is: say, to bind a rethem. Some say: they go into exile, and one walking in exile is not on a chariot. And in my opinion: Where are your words, O Lachish — you who would say in the days of your tranquility, 'Harness the chariot'?!" "<b>For in you were found</b> — This Lachish was adjacent to the tribes of Judah, and she learned from their ways, and from her the daughter of Zion learned."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:37.448785548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}